cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "watchdogspec: watchdog and liveness supervision as a checkable specification"
abstract: >-
  Reads a declared watchdog and liveness specification from YAML - a
  supervisor with its poll period, release jitter and declaration overhead;
  escalation ladders of log, notify, restart_task, safe_mode and reset rungs
  with per-rung worst-case latency and declared recovery cost; and supervised
  tasks with heartbeat periods, jitter bounds and statistics, missed-beat
  tolerances and liveness deadlines - and computes what the declaration
  implies: the worst-case detection latency per task, which rung of each
  escalation ladder can be reached before the deadline, the false-trip rate
  implied by the declared jitter statistics, and twelve ways in which such a
  declaration can contradict itself, including a missed-beat tolerance that
  permits a silence longer than the deadline it is declared to protect. The
  closed-form worst case is cross-checked against a seeded discrete-event
  simulation of heartbeat arrivals. Deterministic, with no learned component.
  It checks a declaration for internal consistency and says nothing about
  whether the declaration matches the system it describes. Research-grade;
  not flight-qualified, not certified, not approved for operational aerospace
  use.
version: 0.1.0
